-- New admin-curated template: "Experimental Determination of Acceleration Due to Gravity"
-- (Physics Practical Workbook: the grandfather, the falling mangoes and "bodies fall at about 10 m/s²").
-- A separate experiment from the existing "Simple Pendulum" (template 12 and its copies are untouched).
--
-- Reuses the pendulum lab (VirtualLabScenePendulum.vue) with render_component 'pendulum_gravity' and the
-- bob prop experiment = 'determine_g', which switches that scene to this practical's configuration:
-- Earth's real g (9.81), the same 50 g bob throughout, lengths 0.100-0.600 m on a 65 cm rule, length
-- measured to the centre of the bob (thread / top-of-bob clicks are refused with a warning), small-angle
-- release check (> 10 degrees warns; the release step accepts up to 10), a 0.01 s stopwatch with a live
-- "n / 20" oscillation counter, reset-before-timing and let-it-settle checks, a read-out refused unless
-- exactly 20 oscillations were timed, and a stand that, if knocked, makes the swing elliptical until
-- steadied. The swing is a real damped simulation, so t comes from the student's own timing.
--
-- The student types t for each length into the results table (VirtualLabGravityAnalysis.vue): T = t/20
-- and T^2 are worked out with the working shown; they plot T^2 against l themselves
-- (VirtualLabStudentGraph.vue), find S = dT^2/dl and g = 4 pi^2 / S, say whether it supports 10 m/s^2,
-- write a conclusion, choose errors/precautions and get a 17-criterion assessment. Each stopwatch
-- reading is also kept as a 'Timing l = ... m' calculation entry, to check the typed times against.
-- Safe to re-run.

SELECT
    'Experimental Determination of Acceleration Due to Gravity', (SELECT id FROM subjects WHERE name = 'PHY' LIMIT 1), 'Mechanics: Acceleration due to gravity', 'physics', 'intermediate', NULL,
    'To determine the value of acceleration due to gravity, g, using a simple pendulum.',
    'An old man and his grandson, who had grown up with his parents in the city, were very hungry after working in a garden. While resting under a mango tree, a ripe mango fell from the tree.\nThe grandson became excited because he wanted to get more ripe mangoes to eat before proceeding home for lunch. His grandfather advised him that if he could climb up the tree and shake the branches, the ripe mangoes would fall to the ground. The grandson did exactly that and many ripe mangoes fell to the ground.\nWhile eating with his grandfather, the grandson told him that their Physics teacher had explained that mangoes fall from trees because of the force of gravity acting on them, and that bodies fall freely at approximately 10 m/s².\nThe old man wanted to know how the teacher arrived at this value, and challenged his grandson to prove experimentally that bodies fall freely at approximately 10 m/s². The grandson therefore decides to use a pendulum experiment to determine the acceleration due to gravity.',
    'One piece of thread (about 110.0 cm), one pendulum bob, one metre rule, one retort stand with clamp, one stopwatch/stop clock, two small pieces of wood.',
    'None (all apparatus is simulated).',
    'Keep the angle of swing small; make sure the retort stand is stable and the bob swings in one vertical plane; avoid draughts from doors, windows and fans.',
    '[{"key":"bob1","object_type":"specimen","position":{"x":-0.8,"y":0,"z":0},"props":{"length_cm":30,"mass_g":50,"experiment":"determine_g"}},{"key":"ruler1","object_type":"ruler","position":{"x":0.8,"y":0,"z":0.8}},{"key":"stopwatch1","object_type":"stopwatch","position":{"x":0.8,"y":0,"z":-0.8}}]',
    'Does your experimental value of g support the statement that bodies fall freely at approximately 10 m/s²?',
    40.00, 1, 'published', '2d', 'pendulum_gravity', 'physics_gravity_pendulum', 1
FROM DUAL
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM `virtual_lab_experiments` WHERE `template_key` = 'physics_gravity_pendulum');

SET @g_id = (SELECT id FROM `virtual_lab_experiments` WHERE `template_key` = 'physics_gravity_pendulum' LIMIT 1);

DELETE FROM `virtual_lab_steps` WHERE `experiment_id` = @g_id;

VALUES (@g_id, 1, 'T squared against l', 'length_m', 'period_squared_s2', 'Length, l (m)', 'Period squared, T^2 (s^2)', 'scatter', 0, 6, 1, 0)
ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE `enabled` = VALUES(`enabled`), `title` = VALUES(`title`), `x_column` = VALUES(`x_column`), `y_column` = VALUES(`y_column`),
    `x_label` = VALUES(`x_label`), `y_label` = VALUES(`y_label`), `graph_type` = VALUES(`graph_type`), `allow_axis_change` = VALUES(`allow_axis_change`),
    `min_points` = VALUES(`min_points`), `show_best_fit` = VALUES(`show_best_fit`), `manual_plot` = VALUES(`manual_plot`);
